course: dictionary
lesson: 159
title: The afternoon
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The afternoon is the part of the day after midday (12 o'clock) and before evening. You can use the word to say when something happens, like «in the afternoon», «this afternoon» or «on Saturday afternoon».
explain: The word can also be a greeting. When you meet someone in the afternoon, you can say «Good afternoon». You would not say it at breakfast or at bedtime, because the greeting is for the afternoon time.
explain: Words from other languages can share the same idea. In Chinese, «xiàwǔ» means afternoon, and it literally means "after noon". The clue is in the word itself: after + noon gives afternoon.
fact: The afternoon comes after midday (12 o'clock) and before evening.
fact: «Good afternoon» is a greeting used in the afternoon.
fact: Times in the afternoon are written p.m., as in 3 p.m.
fact: «Being hungry makes it harder to think and learn in the afternoon.» This is why a school may help a child who has no lunch.
fact: Regional words: «arvo» (Australia) means afternoon; «xiàwǔ» (Chinese) means afternoon.
exercise: «Being hungry makes it harder to think and learn in the afternoon.» When is the afternoon? | Late at night, after bedtime | Just after breakfast | Before midday, when the sun first rises | * After midday and before evening
exercise: Which time is in the afternoon? | * 3 p.m. | 11 a.m. | 9 a.m. | 6 a.m.
exercise: When do you say «Good afternoon»? | At bedtime | When you wake up at night | At breakfast | * When you meet someone in the afternoon
test: An Aussie says, «See you at the arvo.» What does arvo mean? | Lunch time only | * Afternoon | Midnight | Morning
test: The afternoon starts after which time? | Midnight | * Midday, 12 o'clock | Bedtime | Dawn
exam: Jayden says, «We start this afternoon.» When does the lesson start? | Tomorrow morning | At midnight | Last week | * Later today, after midday
